Z||000000||grinthock||08-30-2001||10:20 PM||||Hey everyone (and skitime!)<P>Ok some of you have read my issues over the last week.... So far here is what's been fixed<P>Clogged EGR Tube<BR>replaced EGR Valve<BR>Replaced cracked front manifold<BR>new plugs<BR>new wires<BR>new cap<BR>new rotor<P><BR>All that's been done, drove her tonight and she is runnin pretty nice, took her out on the highway and then back home to see if they are still glowing.  They are not as RED HOT as they were before but they ARE glowing a bit.  Now define glowing, what kind of color, with these if you look into the engine bay you might miss it, (we are talking very dark) but if you look for it, they ARE glowing but not NEAR as much as before.  <P>I know it's hard to guess...  Anyone have ideas?  Car SEEMS to run ok, I am thinking vaccum leak but I have no idea where to start on that one, I confirmed that the EGR is operating.  The ECM isn't throwing codes.<P>Justin.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||08-30-2001||10:39 PM||||gut the cat<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-30-2001||10:48 PM||||Ray;<P><BR>   We have emission controls here, the car comes up for a test in December.  The Cat is new.  It was put on just a little while ago, but I am thinking BECAUSE it was running rich before that it's now melted or something....   What does anyone else think on this?   Obviously it's gotta see a shop to get the cat gutted or replaced right?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000003||85gted||08-30-2001||10:51 PM||||to much retarded timing will make one run to hot, too much or unburned fuel will fire up in the exaust and or restricted exhaust as quoted earler in a sort of a way. 85gted <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Hey everyone (and skitime!)<P>Ok some of you have read my issues over the last week.... So far here is what's been fixed<P>Clogged EGR Tube<BR>replaced EGR Valve<BR>Replaced cracked front manifold<BR>new plugs<BR>new wires<BR>new cap<BR>new rotor<P><BR>All that's been done, drove her tonight and she is runnin pretty nice, took her out on the highway and then back home to see if they are still glowing.  They are not as RED HOT as they were before but they ARE glowing a bit.  Now define glowing, what kind of color, with these if you look into the engine bay you might miss it, (we are talking very dark) but if you look for it, they ARE glowing but not NEAR as much as before.  <P>I know it's hard to guess...  Anyone have ideas?  Car SEEMS to run ok, I am thinking vaccum leak but I have no idea where to start on that one, I confirmed that the EGR is operating.  The ECM isn't throwing codes.<P>Justin.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||08-30-2001||10:53 PM||||At night, mine get a dull orange color to them. You can tell they are glowing, but it's not totally orange, you can see some dark spots on the metal still where the pits and rustyness are in daylight.||||reg||1
